  - `/api/compat/v1` contract (no `/compatibility` suffix): GET is probe-only (rejects request bodies) and returns `{ok:true,schema:"v1"}`; POST is the compat computation surface with request-shape rules (reject mixed id+payload patterns) and strict id validation against `UID_RE` (invalid IDs return an `invalid_json` error envelope with a 400 status). Production-like posture (`APP_ENV`, or `ENGINE_ENV` when `APP_ENV` is blank, normalizes to `prod`, `production` or `live`) returns 404 with `ERR_NOT_FOUND`; otherwise the route and every path under it are served only when `APP_ENV` is exactly `dev`, `test` or `local`, and any other value, unset included, returns 403 `ERR_WRITER_FORBIDDEN` (`Cache-Control: no-store`, no `ETag`) before any computation, database read or vendor call; `ENGINE_ENV` never admits (HDE-CRD-0003 S03; implementation in `engine/http/compat_handler.py`; id regex in `engine/compat/ordering.py`). `run_flask_dev.sh` sets `APP_ENV=dev` only when `APP_ENV` and `ENGINE_ENV` are both unset or empty; `run_flask.py` sets neither. Endpoint catalog entry is POST-only, `internal_admin`, `a7_eligible: false`, and `env_gate` is non-empty (`docs/ENDPOINTS_CATALOG.json` + `.sha256`).
